title: Entra ID Impossible Travel With MFA Satisfied By Existing Token
id: 7e0a9c41-5b2d-4f6e-9a13-0d50a2026it2
status: experimental
description: Identity Protection impossible-travel or unfamiliar-sign-in-properties detection where the second sign-in did not perform a fresh MFA challenge (MFA satisfied by claim in token) — first visible symptom of session/refresh-token theft (T1550.001).
author: Eswar Mahalingam (GraySentinel DSOU, candidate 13)
date: 2026-09-17
references:
  - https://learn.microsoft.com/entra/id-protection/concept-identity-protection-risks
  - https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1550/001/
tags:
  - attack.defense_evasion
  - attack.t1550.001
  - attack.t1078.004
logsource:
  product: azure
  service: signinlogs
detection:
  risk:
    RiskEventTypes|contains:
      - 'impossibleTravel'
      - 'unfamiliarFeatures'
  success:
    ResultType: 0
  no_fresh_mfa:
    AuthenticationDetails|contains:
      - 'previously satisfied'
      - 'claim in the token'
  condition: risk and success and no_fresh_mfa
falsepositives:
  - Corporate VPN / SASE egress in another region (allow-list company egress IPs)
  - Mobile carrier NAT geolocating to a distant city
level: high
